                                "example_id": "272e24cc-89c2-4669-9a06-579432e06f92",
                                "sense_id": "04f6fc5a-8f89-3576-9518-544b03203699",
                                "text": "It might seem that Mr. Holl, whose initial sketches are glorious watercolors, was an unlikely candidate for a job that is all about hydrodynamics. But he credits much of his inspiration to repeated meetings with engineers -- as many as 30 at a time -- to discuss topics like \"flocculation\" (the process by which particles form coagulated masses, or flocs)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2bd2b928-f2f3-3c07-93c2-c83fafbbd20e",
                        "entry_id": "33c0f36e-7ea6-3303-b0af-d32ef5f551a6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A flocculant, as used in swimming pools to make particles clump together so they are trapped by the filter."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "informal",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5bced717-aadc-4ed0-a590-f2c1bd67ea7c",
                                "sense_id": "2bd2b928-f2f3-3c07-93c2-c83fafbbd20e",
                                "text": "This can happen for a few reasons, such as adding too much floc or adding too much algaecide prior to floccing."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
